The data in this directory (and its copies under app/public/data/ and
app/src/data/) is licensed separately from the source code.

Border data (boundaries.json, corrections-geometry.json) derives from
CShapes 2.0 (Schvitz et al.) and, except for the parts noted below, is
therefore distributed under
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode

Non-commercial use only. Attribution required. Adaptations must be shared
under the same license. Modifications are described per feature in the
`source`, `status` and `note` fields, and in scripts/boundary-corrections.js.

Two other sources in the border data keep their own terms:

- The West Bank Areas A/B/C come from UN OCHA / HDX "Oslo Agreement"
  Areas A/B/C (West Bank):
      https://data.humdata.org/dataset/state-of-palestine-other-0-0-0-0-0
  They are distributed under the legacy HumanitarianResponse.info terms,
  not a Creative Commons licence: non-commercial use with credit to
  UN OCHA (derivative works are permitted subject to the inclusion of
  credit to the source; see scripts/extract-correction-geometry.js).
  Carried in each feature's `geometry_source`.
- Some corrected border points (the wells and capes that treaties name)
  are located with GeoNames gazetteer coordinates, CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), https://www.geonames.org/
  (used in scripts/extract-correction-geometry.js).

Event text (extracts) comes from Wikipedia and remains under CC BY-SA 4.0
with attribution to the article authors; see NOTICE at the repository root.

Full credits: ../NOTICE
